\import{fcap-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\taxon{Example}
\title{A null-frame Spin transvection and a radical shear}

\p{Let #{K} be a field in which #{2} is invertible and take the
three-dimensional quadratic space

##{Q(au+bv+cz)=ab+c^2.}

Thus #{u,v} are null, #{B_Q(u,v)=1}, #{Q(z)=1}, and #{z} is orthogonal to
their hyperbolic plane. For #{w=tz}, the preceding lift and action become

##{\begin{gathered}
L_t=1+t\widehat z\widehat u
     =\widehat z\,\widehat{(z+tu)},\\
E_t(u)=u,\qquad E_t(z)=z-2tu,\qquad
E_t(v)=v+tz-t^2u.
\end{gathered}}

Both factors in the displayed product have quadratic value #{1}. Hence the
pair criterion puts #{L_t} directly in the actual Spin group, including at
#{t=0}
\leanref/tauceti{CliffordAlgebra.ι_mul_ι_mem_spinGroup_of_norm_mul_norm_eq_one}.
In coordinates #{(a,c,b)} the transformation is

##{E_t=
\begin{pmatrix}
1&-2t&-t^2\\
0&1&t\\
0&0&1
\end{pmatrix}.}

Substitution gives #{Q(E_t x)=Q(x)}, while multiplication gives
#{E_sE_t=E_{s+t}} and #{L_sL_t=L_{s+t}}. At #{t=1/2},

##{z\longmapsto z-u,\qquad
v\longmapsto v+\frac12z-\frac14u,}

and composing this map with itself gives
#{z\mapsto z-2u} and #{v\mapsto v+z-u}. For #{t\ne0}, the vector action has
#{(E_t-1)^2v=-2t^2u} and #{(E_t-1)^3=0}, although the Clifford increment
satisfies #{(L_t-1)^2=0}. Over #{\mathbb R}, this is the null frame inside
the split model of \ref{fcap-002I}; over every stated field it is a concrete
element of the spinor-norm kernel in \ref{fcap-0023}.}

\p{There is also a precise radical comparison. On the degenerate real form

##{Q_{\mathrm{PGA}}(ar+xe+yf)=x^2+y^2}

the line #{\mathbb Rr} is radical. With #{u=r} and #{w=te}, the same
ring-level transvection formula gives

##{\begin{gathered}
L_t=1+t\widehat e\widehat r
    =\widehat e\,\widehat{(e+tr)},\\
E_t(r)=r,\qquad E_t(e)=e-2tr,\qquad E_t(f)=f.
\end{gathered}}

The nondegenerate packaged Spin-transvection theorem does not apply here.
Nevertheless this particular lift still belongs to the vector-generated Spin
carrier, because both displayed factors have quadratic value #{1}; the pair
criterion itself needs no nondegeneracy. The quadratic action term vanishes
because #{B_Q(r,-)=0}, and now #{(E_t-1)^2=0}. This retains the original
degenerate Clifford algebra rather than replacing it by the radical quotient
of \ref{fcap-002C}. It does not identify the shear with a particular PGA
point translation, motor parameter, dual encoding, or orientation
convention.}
